ed arcaded ramp of many arches climbs from town to the sanctuary and the view back over the roofs.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":10,"urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicenza","https://www.thecrazytourist.com/15-best-things-vicenza-italy/","https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vicenza"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Walk the Palladian route along Corso Palladio","type":"activity","detail":"One straight street strings together the palaces he built, shops and cafes filling the ground floors.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":10,"urls":["https://www.vicenzae.org/en/","https://www.thecrazytourist.com/15-best-things-vicenza-italy/","https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vicenza"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Santa Corona","type":"experience","detail":"A brick Gothic church holding Bellini and Veronese paintings, and the tomb of Palladio himself.","evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":10,"urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicenza","https://www.thecrazytourist.com/15-best-things-vicenza-italy/","https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vicenza"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Baccala alla vicentina and a Colli Berici wine","type":"experience","detail":"Salt cod stewed slowly with milk and onion is the city dish, poured alongside wines from the hills south.","evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":10,"urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicenza","https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vicenza","https://www.vicenzae.org/en/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Palazzo Chiericati","type":"activity","detail":"Another Palladio front, now the city art gallery, with northern Italian painting inside.","evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":10,"urls":["https://www.britannica.com/place/Vicenza-Italy","https://www.findingtheuniverse.com/things-to-do-in-vicenza/","https://notaboutthemiles.com/things-to-do-in-vicenza-italy/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Campo Marzo","type":"activity","sources":["wikidata","wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":2,"so